  "bench_e2e_routing_poc": {
    "tags": ["e2e", "prototype", "routing", "cold-index"],
    "description": "Benchmark-only 8-Mbp segment-routing feasibility sweep. Router-decision timing excludes the separately timed coverage analysis. Whole-segment byte metrics are batch-union upper bounds; one explicit full-scan fallback makes that upper bound 100% by design. Separate directory-range partition-touch metrics assign each query only to its selected segments. Primary truth is maximum overlap, material overlap is >=max(k,ceil(1% truth span)), and adversarial ambiguity explicitly full-scans. Full 2/4-Gbp global max-occ sizing and production-loader acceptance remain blocked; the small repeat is candidate-fixture-only. Compact-layout counters are arithmetic payload/6-KiB logical-row models, not implemented codec, PostgreSQL throughput, or GPU lookup claims; prefix16/suffix48 keeps the full exact hash and local32 stores (segment-local position << 1)|strand. No Paper-ntHash compatibility or performance claim is made.",
    "fast": false,
    "concurrency": {"bench_lock": true, "concurrency": false},
    "iteration_order": {"mode": "interleaved_seeded", "seed": 370},
